{
 "note": "Recorded October 6, 2026 by the designer. Each case: the beats and bible the director saw, and its 3 attempts with the validator errors. Used by Wave I item I4 (salvage).",
 "cases": {
  "story_overdue_book_cold": {
   "beats": [
    {
     "i": 0,
     "word_start": 0,
     "word_end": 5,
     "start_ms": 0,
     "end_ms": 2800,
     "text": "The book that came back"
    },
    {
     "i": 1,
     "word_start": 5,
     "word_end": 21,
     "start_ms": 2800,
     "end_ms": 7675,
     "text": "As a grandmother of three, I thought I had seen every excuse for a late book."
    },
    {
     "i": 2,
     "word_start": 21,
     "word_end": 35,
     "start_ms": 7675,
     "end_ms": 13488,
     "text": "I'm also the only librarian in Alder Creek, Oregon, a town of 2,300 people,"
    },
    {
     "i": 3,
     "word_start": 35,
     "word_end": 46,
     "start_ms": 13488,
     "end_ms": 18575,
     "text": "one stoplight, and a library the size of a two-car garage."
    },
    {
     "i": 4,
     "word_start": 46,
     "word_end": 56,
     "start_ms": 18575,
     "end_ms": 23500,
     "text": "Last October, a padded envelope arrived with no return address."
    },
    {
     "i": 5,
     "word_start": 56,
     "word_end": 68,
     "start_ms": 23500,
     "end_ms": 27975,
     "text": "The postmark said Portland, which meant nothing to me at the time."
    },
    {
     "i": 6,
     "word_start": 68,
     "word_end": 78,
     "start_ms": 27975,
     "end_ms": 31238,
     "text": "Inside was a hardcover novel called The Long Way Home,"
    },
    {
     "i": 7,
     "word_start": 78,
     "word_end": 92,
     "start_ms": 31238,
     "end_ms": 36850,
     "text": "wrapped in a grocery bag. The checkout card was still in its paper pocket."
    },
    {
     "i": 8,
     "word_start": 92,
     "word_end": 109,
     "start_ms": 36850,
     "end_ms": 44550,
     "text": "It had been borrowed on March 9, 1983, and it was due back on March 23, 1983."
    },
    {
     "i": 9,
     "word_start": 109,
     "word_end": 118,
     "start_ms": 44550,
     "end_ms": 50800,
     "text": "Under the book was a stack of cash: $1,554.60."
    },
    {
     "i": 10,
     "word_start": 118,
     "word_end": 122,
     "start_ms": 50800,
     "end_ms": 52825,
     "text": "I counted it twice."
    },
    {
     "i": 11,
     "word_start": 122,
     "word_end": 149,
     "start_ms": 52825,
     "end_ms": 60800,
     "text": "Our late fee is ten cents a day, and when I did the math on a calculator, the fine came out to exactly that, to the penny."
    },
    {
     "i": 12,
     "word_start": 149,
     "word_end": 171,
     "start_ms": 60800,
     "end_ms": 67925,
     "text": "There was a note in shaky blue ink: \"Sorry it took so long. Please give the money to whoever needs it most.\""
    },
    {
     "i": 13,
     "word_start": 171,
     "word_end": 187,
     "start_ms": 67925,
     "end_ms": 74200,
     "text": "My coworker Marisol looked at the cash and said, \"Either that's a confession or a ransom.\""
    },
    {
     "i": 14,
     "word_start": 187,
     "word_end": 197,
     "start_ms": 74200,
     "end_ms": 78000,
     "text": "The checkout card had one name on it: R. Okafor."
    },
    {
     "i": 15,
     "word_start": 197,
     "word_end": 214,
     "start_ms": 78000,
     "end_ms": 83975,
     "text": "But when I opened the book, the margins were full of pencil notes in two different handwritings."
    },
    {
     "i": 16,
     "word_start": 214,
     "word_end": 225,
     "start_ms": 83975,
     "end_ms": 88575,
     "text": "One was small and neat. The other was big and messy."
    },
    {
     "i": 17,
     "word_start": 225,
     "word_end": 234,
     "start_ms": 88575,
     "end_ms": 92300,
     "text": "They were arguing about the story, chapter by chapter."
    },
    {
     "i": 18,
     "word_start": 234,
     "word_end": 248,
     "start_ms": 92300,
     "end_ms": 98550,
     "text": "The messy writer signed every note \"R.\" The neat writer signed every note \"J.\""
    },
    {
     "i": 19,
     "word_start": 248,
     "word_end": 267,
     "start_ms": 98550,
     "end_ms": 106100,
     "text": "\"The ending is too sad, \"R. wrote on page 40. \"The ending is the point, \"J. wrote back underneath."
    },
    {
     "i": 20,
     "word_start": 267,
     "word_end": 280,
     "start_ms": 106100,
     "end_ms": 110975,
     "text": "I spent a weekend in our basement with the old card catalog boxes."
    },
    {
     "i": 21,
     "word_start": 280,
     "word_end": 293,
     "start_ms": 110975,
     "end_ms": 116750,
     "text": "The library kept every checkout card from before we went digital in 1998."
    },
    {
     "i": 22,
     "word_start": 293,
     "word_end": 308,
     "start_ms": 116750,
     "end_ms": 121688,
     "text": "I found that The Long Way Home had been checked out 26 times in 1982,"
    },
    {
     "i": 23,
     "word_start": 308,
     "word_end": 318,
     "start_ms": 121688,
     "end_ms": 126825,
     "text": "every two weeks, alternating between R. Okafor and J. Lind."
    },
    {
     "i": 24,
     "word_start": 318,
     "word_end": 337,
     "start_ms": 126825,
     "end_ms": 134125,
     "text": "They had never written a word to each other anywhere but in that book. The library was their mailbox."
    },
    {
     "i": 25,
     "word_start": 337,
     "word_end": 355,
     "start_ms": 134125,
     "end_ms": 140350,
     "text": "The last note in the book was from J., inside the back cover: \"Same time next week? J.\""
    },
    {
     "i": 26,
     "word_start": 355,
     "word_end": 359,
     "start_ms": 140350,
     "end_ms": 142375,
     "text": "There was no reply."
    },
    {
     "i": 27,
     "word_start": 359,
     "word_end": 369,
     "start_ms": 142375,
     "end_ms": 147975,
     "text": "After March 1983, R. Okafor never checked out another book."
    },
    {
     "i": 28,
     "word_start": 369,
     "word_end": 382,
     "start_ms": 147975,
     "end_ms": 152938,
     "text": "J. Lind was easy to find. June Lind still lives on Cedar Street,"
    },
    {
     "i": 29,
     "word_start": 382,
     "word_end": 394,
     "start_ms": 152938,
     "end_ms": 157500,
     "text": "four blocks from the library, and she still comes in every Tuesday."
    },
    {
     "i": 30,
     "word_start": 394,
     "word_end": 414,
     "start_ms": 157500,
     "end_ms": 164250,
     "text": "When I showed her the book, she sat down very slowly. She told me she never learned who R. was."
    },
    {
     "i": 31,
     "word_start": 414,
     "word_end": 434,
     "start_ms": 164250,
     "end_ms": 171813,
     "text": "She waited at the return desk every Tuesday for a month in 1983, and then she stopped waiting. She married,"
    },
    {
     "i": 32,
     "word_start": 434,
     "word_end": 443,
     "start_ms": 171813,
     "end_ms": 176375,
     "text": "raised two sons, and lost her husband in 2015."
    },
    {
     "i": 33,
     "word_start": 443,
     "word_end": 454,
     "start_ms": 176375,
     "end_ms": 180475,
     "text": "\"I always assumed R. just got bored of me, \"she said."
    },
    {
     "i": 34,
     "word_start": 454,
     "word_end": 468,
     "start_ms": 180475,
     "end_ms": 186350,
     "text": "I posted on the town's Facebook page asking if anyone remembered an R. Okafor."
    },
    {
     "i": 35,
     "word_start": 468,
     "word_end": 482,
     "start_ms": 186350,
     "end_ms": 191800,
     "text": "Three days later, a man named Robert Okafor sent me a message from Portland."
    },
    {
     "i": 36,
     "word_start": 482,
     "word_end": 487,
     "start_ms": 191800,
     "end_ms": 194875,
     "text": "He was 19 in 1983."
    },
    {
     "i": 37,
     "word_start": 487,
     "word_end": 494,
     "start_ms": 194875,
     "end_ms": 197150,
     "text": "His father lost his job that March,"
    },
    {
     "i": 38,
     "word_start": 494,
     "word_end": 515,
     "start_ms": 197150,
     "end_ms": 204225,
     "text": "and the family moved to Portland in one weekend. He took the book by accident in a box of his things."
    },
    {
     "i": 39,
     "word_start": 515,
     "word_end": 541,
     "start_ms": 204225,
     "end_ms": 211825,
     "text": "By the time he found it, he was too embarrassed to send it back, and too shy to write to someone he only knew as J."
    },
    {
     "i": 40,
     "word_start": 541,
     "word_end": 560,
     "start_ms": 211825,
     "end_ms": 217300,
     "text": "He said he kept the book for 42 years because it was the only thing he had of her."
    },
    {
     "i": 41,
     "word_start": 560,
     "word_end": 575,
     "start_ms": 217300,
     "end_ms": 222475,
     "text": "He finally mailed it when his doctor told him to put his affairs in order."
    },
    {
     "i": 42,
     "word_start": 575,
     "word_end": 586,
     "start_ms": 222475,
     "end_ms": 226575,
     "text": "He sent the money so the library would not be cheated."
    },
    {
     "i": 43,
     "word_start": 586,
     "word_end": 596,
     "start_ms": 226575,
     "end_ms": 230375,
     "text": "I asked him if he wanted to return it himself."
    },
    {
     "i": 44,
     "word_start": 596,
     "word_end": 599,
     "start_ms": 230375,
     "end_ms": 231938,
     "text": "The following Tuesday,"
    },
    {
     "i": 45,
     "word_start": 599,
     "word_end": 618,
     "start_ms": 231938,
     "end_ms": 238550,
     "text": "a man in a gray coat walked into the library holding a canvas bag that had seen better decades."
    },
    {
     "i": 46,
     "word_start": 618,
     "word_end": 633,
     "start_ms": 238550,
     "end_ms": 244400,
     "text": "June was at the return desk. Neither of them said anything for a long time."
    },
    {
     "i": 47,
     "word_start": 633,
     "word_end": 648,
     "start_ms": 244400,
     "end_ms": 249775,
     "text": "Then Robert put the book on the counter and said, \"Sorry. It's a little overdue.\""
    },
    {
     "i": 48,
     "word_start": 648,
     "word_end": 666,
     "start_ms": 249775,
     "end_ms": 257325,
     "text": "I stamped it RETURNED with that day's date. It was the first stamp on that card since 1983."
    },
    {
     "i": 49,
     "word_start": 666,
     "word_end": 675,
     "start_ms": 257325,
     "end_ms": 260650,
     "text": "They had coffee across the street for three hours."
    },
    {
     "i": 50,
     "word_start": 675,
     "word_end": 688,
     "start_ms": 260650,
     "end_ms": 264525,
     "text": "Now they read the same book every month, each with their own copy,"
    },
    {
     "i": 51,
     "word_start": 688,
     "word_end": 708,
     "start_ms": 264525,
     "end_ms": 272025,
     "text": "and they still write in the margins before they trade. June says R. still thinks every ending is too sad."
    },
    {
     "i": 52,
     "word_start": 708,
     "word_end": 721,
     "start_ms": 272025,
     "end_ms": 278600,
     "text": "We used the $1,554.60 to build a reading nook by the front window,"
    },
    {
     "i": 53,
     "word_start": 721,
     "word_end": 727,
     "start_ms": 278600,
     "end_ms": 281400,
     "text": "with two chairs facing each other."
    },
    {
     "i": 54,
     "word_start": 727,
     "word_end": 737,
     "start_ms": 281400,
     "end_ms": 286325,
     "text": "Marisol made the sign. It says \"The Long Way Home.\""
    },
    {
     "i": 55,
     "word_start": 737,
     "word_end": 756,
     "start_ms": 286325,
     "end_ms": 291500,
     "text": "The fine was ten cents a day. It turned out to be the cheapest thing in the whole story."
    }
   ],
